==German==

===Etymology===
Ultimately from {{etyl|gem-pro|de}} {{recons|draugiz|lang=gem-pro}}, from {{etyl|ine-pro|de}} {{recons|dʰerǵʰ-||to strengthen; become hard or solid|lang=ine-pro}}, from {{recons|dʰer-||to hold, hold fast, support|lang=ine-pro}}. Compare Dutch {{term|droog|lang=nl}}, West Frisian {{term|droech|lang=fy}}, English {{term|dry|lang=en}}.

